TimeScale [SimTalk]
Sets the time scale of the GanttChart designated by <Path>. Plant Simulation applies this value when
opening the GanttChart.
Remarks
The unit of the time scale is logical pixels per second. For a time scale of 0.5 Plant Simulation shows a
Gantt event with a duration of 60 seconds with a bar of a length of 30 logical pixels.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.TimeScale:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real.
Specify 0 to use the default time scaling.
Example
MyGanttChart.TimeScale := 2.5
See also
Show Chart [button] - GanttChart
SankeyDiagram
SankeyDiagram [object]
Use the object SankeyDiagram for visualizing the Sankey flows of parts, the Sankey flows of Workers, who
walk freely within the area or walk on FootPaths, and the Sankey flows of AGVs driving freely within the
area of the model.
Image
TimeScale [SimTalk]
11-4860 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Description
To show Sankey flows of class objects, drag the classes Part, Container, Worker, WorkerPool, Transporter,
or AGVPool from the Class Library over the picture of the SankeyDiagram and drop it it there.
To show Sankey flows of individual instances of Part, Container, Worker, WorkerPool, Transporter,
or AGVPool, type the name of this instance into the cell of the list on the tab Objects, for
example .MUs.Part:3.
To show a tooltip with information about the SankeyDiagram, hover with the mouse over it.
To change the length of the graphic and the anchor points of the SankeyDiagram, click Show
Manipulators 
  on the Edit ribbon tab or press M on the keyboard.
Add the Object to the Simulation Model
To add the object SankeyDiagram to your simulation model, click 
  Manage Class Library > Basic
Objects > UserInterface > SankeyDiagram on the Home ribbon tab.
See also
Show Part Flows in a SankeyDiagram
Show AGV Flows in a SankeyDiagram
Display a SankeyDiagram in the HtmlReport
